      "message": "Before this change, tests that declared uniforms that didn\u0027t match wgsl\u0027s layout (or required std140 emulation) wouldn\u0027t work correctly. This led to two behaviors: just using wgsl\u0027s types and it cechnically compiles but isn\u0027t what real sksl would generate (e.g. float2x2 was just being transformed to a mat2 w/o extra alignment padding), or it actually failed to compile in tint.\n\nBecause of the bind/group ordering change, almost every wgsl test output got modified. The benign changes are just those with 1-2 diffed lines.  Many fewer tests actually had the substantial rewrite to apply the amulation.\n\nAt this point, I believe all wgsl files emitted pass tint compilation now.",
